---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout 
  title="How to Choose a Tour in China: What to Know Before You Book | YOGOTOCHINA" 
  description="When is a China tour worth it, when is it a trap, and how do you book one without overpaying? A practical guide for foreign travelers, with real mistakes to avoid."
>
  <div style="max-width: 1000px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem 1.5rem;">

    <!-- 返回链接 -->
    <a href="/" style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; margin-bottom: 2rem; color: #6c757d; text-decoration: none; font-size: 0.9rem;">
      <span>←</span> Back to Home
    </a>

    <!-- ===== 标题区 ===== -->
    <div style="margin-bottom: 2rem;">
      <h1 style="font-size: 2.4rem; font-weight: 700; color: #1F2A2E; letter-spacing: -0.5px; margin: 0 0 1rem 0; line-height: 1.2;">
        How to Choose a Tour in China: What to Know Before You Book
      </h1>
      <p style="font-size: 1.1rem; color: #4a4a4a; line-height: 1.7; margin: 0;">
        Most cheap China tours are cheap for a reason: they make money from forced shopping stops. This page explains when a tour is worth it, when it isn't, and how to book one without overpaying.
      </p>
      <p style="font-size: 0.95rem; color: #6c757d; line-height: 1.7; margin: 1rem 0 0 0;">
        Still deciding where to go? Read our <a href="/findway/" style="color: #2D6A4F; font-weight: 600; text-decoration: underline;">China travel routes guide</a> first.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- ===== 三个决策入口 ===== -->
    <h2 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; color: #1F2A2E; margin: 2.5rem 0 1rem 0;">
      Start with your situation
    </h2>

    <div style="display: grid; gap: 1rem; margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">

      <!-- 入口一：想跟团但怕购物团 -->
      <div style="background: #FFFFFF; border: 1px solid #E2E0D4; border-radius: 16px; padding: 1.5rem;">
        <h3 style="font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 700; color: #1F2A2E; margin: 0 0 0.5rem 0;">
          You want a guide, but you don't want a shopping tour
        </h3>
        <p style="font-size: 0.95rem; color: #4a4a4a; line-height: 1.7; margin: 0 0 1rem 0;">
          How to spot a shopping tour before you pay, what a fair price looks like, and which platforms are safe to book through.
        </p>
        <a href="/blog/how-to-choose-a-tour-guide-china/" style="display: inline-block; background: #2D6A4F; color: #FFFFFF; padding: 0.6rem 1.4rem; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; font-size: 0.9rem; font-weight: 600;">
          How to Choose a Tour Guide in China →
        </a>
      </div>

      <!-- 入口二：想自己走 -->
      <div style="background: #FFFFFF; border: 1px solid #E2E0D4; border-radius: 16px; padding: 1.5rem;">
        <h3 style="font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 700; color: #1F2A2E; margin: 0 0 0.5rem 0;">
          You'd rather go independent, but trains and payments worry you
        </h3>
        <p style="font-size: 0.95rem; color: #4a4a4a; line-height: 1.7; margin: 0 0 1rem 0;">
          China is easier to do alone than most people think. High-speed trains, Didi, and Alipay cover almost everything. Here is how to set them up.
        </p>
        <div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.6rem;">
          <a href="/blog/how-to-get-around-china/" style="display: inline-block; background: #2D6A4F; color: #FFFFFF; padding: 0.6rem 1.4rem; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; font-size: 0.9rem; font-weight: 600;">
            How to Get Around China →
          </a>
          <a href="/blog/how-to-pay-in-china/" style="display: inline-block; background: #F0F7F0; color: #2D6A4F; padding: 0.6rem 1.4rem; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; font-size: 0.9rem; font-weight: 600; border: 1px solid #D5E8D5;">
            Payment Guide
          </a>
          <a href="/blog/china-esim-vpn-internet-guide/" style="display: inline-block; background: #F0F7F0; color: #2D6A4F; padding: 0.6rem 1.4rem; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; font-size: 0.9rem; font-weight: 600; border: 1px solid #D5E8D5;">
            eSIM & Internet
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- 入口三：重庆文化体验 -->
      <div style="background: #FFFFFF; border: 1px solid #E2E0D4; border-radius: 16px; padding: 1.5rem;">
        <h3 style="font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 700; color: #1F2A2E; margin: 0 0 0.5rem 0;">
          You're going to Chongqing and want one unforgettable cultural experience
        </h3>
        <p style="font-size: 0.95rem; color: #4a4a4a; line-height: 1.7; margin: 0 0 1rem 0;">
          The Banquet of the Ba Kingdom is a 90-minute royal feast with ancient performances. Here is what it costs, where it is, and how to book it.
        </p>
        <a href="/blog/china-chongqing-banquet-ba-kingdom/" style="display: inline-block; background: #2D6A4F; color: #FFFFFF; padding: 0.6rem 1.4rem; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; font-size: 0.9rem; font-weight: 600;">
          The Ba Kingdom Banquet Guide →
        </a>
      </div>

    </div>

    <!-- ===== Common Mistakes ===== -->
    <h2 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; color: #1F2A2E; margin: 2.5rem 0 1rem 0;">
      Common mistakes when booking a China tour
    </h2>

    <div style="background: #FFF8E7; border-left: 4px solid #C49E3A; border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
      <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 1.2rem; color: #4a4a4a; font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.9;">
        <li style="margin-bottom: 0.8rem;">
          <strong>Booking a tour that costs less than the train ticket and entrance fees combined.</strong> That price gap is not a discount. It is a shopping stop in disguise.
        </li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 0.8rem;">
          <strong>Not asking whether the tour includes shopping stops.</strong> Many tours labeled "no shopping" still list a jade factory or tea house in the small print. Ask before you pay.
        </li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 0.8rem;">
          <strong>Pre-booking everything before you land.</strong> Weather changes, some sights are not worth it, and cancellations cost money. Book only what sells out (Forbidden City, Terracotta Warriors) and buy the rest same-day.
        </li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 0.8rem;">
          <strong>Assuming the guide speaks fluent English.</strong> A licensed guide is not always a fluent one. Confirm the language level before booking, especially for private tours.
        </li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 0.8rem;">
          <strong>Paying the full amount before reading the cancellation policy.</strong> Refund terms matter more than the price. A cheap tour with no refund is more expensive than a fair tour with flexible cancellation.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Picking the wrong Great Wall section.</strong> Badaling is the most crowded. Mutianyu has fewer people and a toboggan, Jinshanling is better for photos, and Jiankou is only for serious hikers.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- ===== 轻咨询出口 ===== -->
    <div style="background: #F0F7F0; border-radius: 16px; padding: 2rem; text-align: center; margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
      <h2 style="font-size: 1.3rem; font-weight: 700; color: #1F2A2E; margin: 0 0 0.5rem 0;">
        Not sure what fits your trip?
      </h2>
      <p style="font-size: 0.95rem; color: #4a4a4a; line-height: 1.7; margin: 0 0 1.2rem 0;">
        Tell me your dates, who's traveling, and what you want to see. I'll point you in the right direction. No booking required.
      </p>
      <a href="mailto:hello@yogotochina.com" style="display: inline-block; background: #2D6A4F; color: #FFFFFF; padding: 0.7rem 1.8rem; border-radius: 30px; text-decoration: none; font-size: 0.95rem; font-weight: 600;">
        Email me →
      </a>
    </div>

    <!-- ===== 底部 Essential Guides ===== -->
    <div style="background: #FFFFFF; border: 1px solid #EDEAE0; border-radius: 16px; padding: 2rem; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
      <h2 style="font-size: 1.2rem; font-weight: 700; color: #1F2A2E; margin: 0 0 1rem 0;">
        Before you book anything
      </h2>
      <p style="font-size: 0.95rem; color: #6c757d; margin: 0 0 1.5rem 0;">
        Make sure your payments, internet, and transport are sorted first. These guides cover everything you need before you fly.
      </p>
      <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 0.75rem;">
        <a href="/blog/china-travel-checklist/" style="display: block; background: #2D6A4F; color: white; padding: 0.6rem 1rem; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.9rem; text-align: center;">Pre-Departure Checklist</a>
        <a href="/blog/how-to-pay-in-china/" style="display: block; background: #F8F6F0; color: #1F2A2E; padding: 0.6rem 1rem; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.9rem; text-align: center; border: 1px solid #EDEAE0;">Payment Guide</a>
        <a href="/blog/china-esim-vpn-internet-guide/" style="display: block; background: #F8F6F0; color: #1F2A2E; padding: 0.6rem 1rem; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.9rem; text-align: center; border: 1px solid #EDEAE0;">eSIM & Internet</a>
        <a href="/blog/how-to-get-around-china/" style="display: block; background: #F8F6F0; color: #1F2A2E; padding: 0.6rem 1rem; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.9rem; text-align: center; border: 1px solid #EDEAE0;">Transport Guide</a>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</Layout>